Margin is an AI tutor a university endorses instead of banning other tools. The policy line is: if you use an AI, use Margin. Harvard CS50 is the precedent.

Students never receive the solution. Help is a hint ladder. Level 1 is one guiding question. Level 2 is a pointer to the professor's materials. Level 3 is a worked example of a different but related problem.

A leak guard checks every draft against the hidden answer key before the student sees it. A scribe labels each turn with the concept, the struggle type, and the hint level. The professor sees class-level patterns first and a "reteach this" card, not a grade.

The default demo subject, until Dr. Lund's real course is confirmed, is intro CS, Python recursion, sum_list.

Four roles come later: Tutor, Guard, Scribe, and Coach. Out of scope this weekend: LMS integration, real auth, multiple courses, essays, and mobile.

The stack for this repo is a Next.js frontend and an Express backend. Do not switch the backend to Python.

This is HackPrinceton Fall 2026. The hard submit deadline is 8:00 AM America/New_York on Sunday, November 15, 2026. The in-person demo is required and capped at 2 minutes. Submit the public GitHub repo only. It was created during the event. Judging criteria are Creativity, Utility, Charity, and Avidity.

Enter exactly one main track: Education. The packet describes Education as projects that make learning more interactive, accessible, or personalized.

Best Overall is automatic, not an entry. Track winners cannot also win Best Overall.

Enter these sub tracks. Amazon, Best Practical AI Innovation: Education is in scope, and the entry needs a working demo, a clear user, and basic docs. Peri, Forward Deployed Challenge: it requires a real client consulted during the weekend, and a student org counts. Include their name, role, and evidence. Do not claim a pilot that is not confirmed. LangChain, Best use of deepagents: enter only if a deepagent is actually in the build. The backend is Express, so do not add this unless asked. Photon messaging agent: enter only if students can message the tutor or the professor gets the log as a message. The voice prize applies only if voice exists. ChatOverflow leaderboard: connect the coding agent while building. That needs no product change and no extra Devpost submission.

Enter Best Rookie only if every team member's first hackathon.

Do not enter CoStar, because it needs their building data. Do not enter Arlequin forensics, Arlequin social-media analysis, Capital One Nessie, Physical AI, or Best Hardware. Salesforce and Scale AI are career-fair only. This packet has no MLH or Gemini prize.
